  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "A hiker\u2019s elevation was recorded over time for $6$ hours, starting from time $t=0$ hours. The following table shows the elevation $E(t)$, in meters, recorded at time $t.$\n\n| $t$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $E(t)$ | $0$ | $200$ | $310$ | $395$ | $450$ | $525$ | $600$ |\n\nApproximate the rate of change of elevation at time $t=1$ using a forward difference approximation. Do not round the answer.\n\nAt $t=1,$ the estimated rate of change is {{field-1}} meters per hour.",
  "worked_solution": "We use the forward difference approximation\n\n$$\n{E}^{\u2032}(t)\u2248\\frac{E(t+h)-E(t)}{h}\n$$\n\nat the point $t=1.$ We choose the step size $h$ to be as small as possible, in this case $h=1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}^{\u2032}(1) & \u2248\\frac{E(1+1)-E(1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{E(2)-E(1)}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{310-200}{1} \\\\  & =110.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, at $t=1$ the rate of change was approximately $110$ meters per hour.",
